### Passes that came back clean

- **Pass 2 (visual sweep):** all 9 crops plus 7 targeted zooms. All 20 aisle corridors probe **100% green end-to-end** (y 268→badge, no gaps). Market action alley continuous `x 220→1050` at y 245–265; front action alley continuous `x 150→860`; south cross-aisle continuous to `x 1050`. Dairy, Deli, Bakery, Produce, Floral, Seafood/Market frontages all green; staff blocks, lease units (National Jewelry, Cricket, Browz, First Convenience Bank, Medical Information Center), restrooms and back-of-house all sealed; checkout lanes sealed with the front alley green both sides. **All 40 culled pockets classified** — dairy cooler, market prep, lease units, Services office, SE service rooms, checkout-lane interiors, U-display-case interiors, and a wall-thickness crevice at `(84,494)-(330,632)` whose bbox merely *contains* the Produce label without covering it. No unexplained pocket.
- **Pass 3 (label probes):** ran exhaustively over all **275** PDF words rather than 10. Every product label has reachable floor within ~1 m. The only words beyond 2 m are outdoor text (Outdoor Sales/Seating, Red Box), the correctly-sealed lease-unit names, staff-side department titles (Bakery 3.2 m, Deli 2.4 m, Dairy 2.5 m — all printed behind their counters, as `exclusions.json` states), and `Rx` (Finding 1).
- **Pass 4 (walk_truth adequacy):** all 16 original assertions passed; now 18 `must` / 16 `must_not`, 0 failures against the fresh grid.
- **Pass 5 (config sanity):** all 5 exclusions and 4 inclusions carry a WHY consistent with the map. No exclusion swallows a product label (only the staff-side `Deli`/`Bakery` titles and `National Jewelry`). The Seafood inclusion opens only the customer alley south of the diagonal case — the case and meat-case interiors stay sealed (verified visually). The aisle-5 inclusion covers a single 26-pt corridor, not a staff room.

### Flagged risk (not a blocker for 189)

`engine.SERVICE_DEPTS` has no `RX` synonym for `PHARMACY`. Store 189's artifacts are correct and its pharmacy is now permanently pinned by walk_truth, so this needs no code change to ship. But any future guide that prints "Rx" will likewise get no anchor, no seal-disk and no VERIFY flag over its pharmacy — worth a one-word vocabulary addition by whoever owns `router/engine.py`. I did not touch it.

`AUDIT CLEAN — store 189 (2 findings fixed)`
